    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "we checked the temp and it's holding steady at 400f for the whole cycle. pressure seems even too. we also checked the paper and it's dry. sometimes it's just one specific area of the print that looks washed out or like the ink just isnt there, even when the rest of the design is fine. any idea why it would be inconsistent like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Inconsistent printing, especially in specific areas, often points to an issue with the sublimation material itself or how it's being applied. Inspect your sublimation printer to ensure the ink density is consistent across the nozzle heads. Additionally, if you are using specific inks or coatings, verify they are compatible with your heat press and transfer paper. Sometimes areas of poor adhesion on the fabric can also cause localized fading.",
      "source": "target",
